    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^3-2x^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p81-q53-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Touches the $x$-axis at $(0,0)$ and crosses at $(2,0)$; the left end points down and the right end points up.",
          "worked": "$$f(x)=x^2(x-2).$$\n\nThe double root at $x=0$ gives a touch at the origin; the single root at $x=2$ gives a crossing. The leading coefficient is positive, so the left end points down and the right end points up. Draw the curve below the $x$-axis on either side of the origin, with a trough between $0$ and $2$, before it crosses at $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
